WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.000
I don't remember jokes and I
don't remember scary stories.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:03.833
Yeah, me either.

00:00:03.833 --> 00:00:05.040
My scary stories are all about

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.540
someone making a bad investment.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.850
Mine are about rabbits
getting killed in my backyard.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:09.683
[Conan] Right.

00:00:09.683 --> 00:00:11.790
Are we talking about
jokes or scary stories?

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:12.623
Scary stories.

00:00:12.623 --> 00:00:13.456
Well, they're the same kind of.

00:00:13.456 --> 00:00:15.759
I remember one joke
that I say all the time.

00:00:15.759 --> 00:00:16.740
What is it?

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.590
What's Beethoven's favorite fruit?

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.430
Oh, wait, wait, wait.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:21.840
I'm sure I've said this to you before.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.520
It's her only joke, I've
heard it many times.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.600
It's my only joke.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.433
Okay, hold on.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:30.960
Watermelon.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.116
Ba-na-na-na.

00:00:32.116 --> 00:00:33.150
You were close!

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:33.983
I knew it.

00:00:33.983 --> 00:00:35.408
No, no, he wasn't close.

00:00:35.408 --> 00:00:36.241
(laughs)

00:00:36.241 --> 00:00:40.170
What he said made no sense at all.

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:42.750
That's like if you asked a dog to explain

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.400
the theory of relativity and it barked

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.633
and you went, close.

00:00:46.663 --> 00:00:49.140
It's E equals MC squared.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.853
Oh!

00:00:50.853 --> 00:00:52.091
What's the dog.

00:00:52.091 --> 00:00:54.794
(laughs)

00:00:54.794 --> 00:00:57.270
Any time I play the guitar

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:59.470
it's gonna make your editing
much more difficult, isn't it?

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:01.260
Yeah, that's right.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.360
What is Wilson Phillips' favorite fruit?

00:01:05.479 --> 00:01:07.290
Guava for one more day.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:10.650
No, you can't do the same idea.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.520
And you also had to think about it,

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.670
'cause you had to think about
what fruit fit in there.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:19.235
I don't know, I'm upset about it.

00:01:19.235 --> 00:01:20.880
(laughs)

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.220
So guava for one more day.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:24.053
Now I have a question.

00:01:24.053 --> 00:01:25.050
You edit these things.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:27.360
Will you edit that out?
Are you kidding?

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:28.710
What will you do to protect yourself?

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.990
I will move that to the front.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:31.823
And put an echo on it.

00:01:31.823 --> 00:01:32.973
That's the opening.

00:01:32.973 --> 00:01:35.056
(laughs)

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:37.193
Look at Sona.

00:01:37.193 --> 00:01:39.445
You're navigating your cup to your mouth.

00:01:39.445 --> 00:01:43.020
like you're landing a
plane in inclement weather.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.380
It's like one of the Apollos
where they have to dock it

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:48.480
and they have to line it up exactly right.

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:51.450
Oh my God, look at that.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:53.730
I didn't realize drinking
would be part of this.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:55.320
You didn't?
I didn't, no.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.390
I would not have been okay with that.

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:59.010
'Cause I knew this would happen.

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.030
You need another one, Conan?

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.595
No, I do not.

00:02:01.595 --> 00:02:06.510
I like to drink slowly and
then I think after one, I quit.

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:08.010
Hi, if you're listening

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:11.160
and you're an impressionable
teen do as Conan does

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:12.690
not as Gourley says,

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.580
and remember Solo Stove

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.830
is the way to keep those
home fires burning.

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:19.687
Yeah, and you could put color packets.

00:02:19.687 --> 00:02:21.267
Are we done?

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:22.100
What do you mean, are you done?

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:22.933
Oh, there's a guitar holder over there.

00:02:22.933 --> 00:02:23.766
Oh, there it is.

00:02:23.766 --> 00:02:25.050
Oh, I didn't see it.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:26.610
I thought they had moved it outta the way.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:28.260
Those are some great ghost stories though.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.093
You know what?

00:02:29.093 --> 00:02:30.030
We don't have any ghost stories.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:32.160
'Cause none of us really
believe in ghosts, right?

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:35.910
Well, I just don't find ghosts scary.

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:38.190
I love true crime.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:40.704
And I find, and you're the same way, Sona,

00:02:40.704 --> 00:02:44.070
I love a true crime story and I find that

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:46.890
to be very eerie or an unsolved murder,

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.633
that kind of stuff freaks me out.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:53.070
I remember when Blair
Witch Project came out.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.200
When something is unsaid or unstated

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.226
or some of those movies like Witch.

00:02:58.226 --> 00:02:59.820
Remember the Witch?
Yes.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.680
Or Midsommar?
Oh yeah.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:02.970
Hereditary.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:05.190
I find movies where something's just off,

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:08.100
but it's not that explicit.
I agree.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.903
That terrifies me.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:13.560
Like in the movie, the Witch,

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:17.040
they can just show some
trees in the distance,

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.840
and they're undulating in the breeze,

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.570
but because of the tone
they've set and the music.

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:22.740
I find that scary.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:26.250
Guys dressed up in a
leather mask with a chainsaw

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:27.488
doesn't do anything for me.

00:03:27.488 --> 00:03:28.321
Terrifies me.

00:03:28.321 --> 00:03:30.720
That does beg the question
though of the big three,

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.750
Michael Myers, Jason
Voorhees and Freddy Kruger

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.610
which are we?
Ooh.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.653
So Freddy's real mouthy.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:40.173
It's gotta be you
That's you.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:41.903
I guess so.

00:03:41.903 --> 00:03:44.040
I never liked those
'cause I never understood

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.000
what the rules were.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.680
I like to know what the rules are.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:48.810
I think you would like the
idea of haunting people

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:49.643
in their dreams.

00:03:49.643 --> 00:03:50.700
I do haunt people in their dreams.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.057
You haunt me in my dreams.

00:03:52.057 --> 00:03:54.473
I think he is Freddy Kreuger.

00:03:54.473 --> 00:03:57.870
Most of my career was spent
literally doing a show

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:01.560
that people fell asleep
to from 12:30 to 1:30.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:06.420
I think I'm in people's
deep, deep unconscious.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:07.800
And I'm wreaking havoc.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:08.700
I think you're Jason,

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:10.620
because he's got a sweet side to him.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:11.453
That's nice.

00:04:11.453 --> 00:04:12.750
Kind of innocence.
Okay.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:13.830
And I think I'm Michael,

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:17.460
'cause I'm mysterious and kind
of enigmatic and charming.

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:18.570
And unkillable.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:19.560
Yeah.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.750
All of us are unkillable.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.070
I can't watch horror stories.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.900
I mean horror movies.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:25.830
It keeps me up at night.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:27.240
But I don't find those scary.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.730
You don't at all, like
even when you were a kid?

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:30.843
The first Halloween?

00:04:33.222 --> 00:04:34.780
I don't think I saw it.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:36.960
Maybe I didn't see the first
Halloween when it came out.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:37.793
Oh, it's so scary.

00:04:37.793 --> 00:04:39.076
I was still in the convent.

00:04:39.076 --> 00:04:41.130
When Final Destination came out,

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.020
my friend's mom had to follow me home

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:44.880
'cause I thought death was after me.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.403
But you having someone
follow you wasn't scary?

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:50.160
You asked your friend
who was wearing a cloak

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.219
to follow you home.

00:04:51.219 --> 00:04:53.790
(laughs)

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:55.650
Your friend who wore a cloak,

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:58.320
'cause it was chilly
and he got cold easily,

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:01.020
and he had just bought a
scythe at the scythe store.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:02.340
Hey, do me a favor.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:03.980
I'm really scared, could
you follow me home?

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:05.063
And he was like, yes I will.

00:05:05.063 --> 00:05:07.470
Because he had terrible asthma.

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.303
This is perfect.

00:05:08.303 --> 00:05:10.320
'Cause we're all basically 10 years apart.

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.840
And I bet our horror movies
don't work for the other

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:15.690
or at least not those that came before us.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:17.040
Exorcist probably scared you.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.780
I think the Omen, the Omen scared me.

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:19.613
Halloween for me.

00:05:19.613 --> 00:05:21.180
And you're saying Final Destination

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:22.380
which doesn't scare me at all.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:23.913
And Blair Witch was really scary.

00:05:23.913 --> 00:05:26.010
Yes. I thought Blair Witch was scary.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:27.630
Giving a shout out to the newer movies,

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.430
I think the newer movies,

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.090
like I said, the Witch,
Hereditary, Midsommar.

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:35.340
Those freak me out.

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:36.413
I think those are brilliant.

00:05:36.413 --> 00:05:40.140
I think the horror they're
doing now is maybe superior.

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:41.340
It's psychological.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:42.840
They call it elevated horror.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:43.673
Yeah.

00:05:43.673 --> 00:05:44.506
That's good.

00:05:44.506 --> 00:05:46.413
We started educating people accidentally.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:50.310
It got sort of useful.

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:51.420
We're a film podcast.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:52.920
Look at us.
Let's turn this around.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:54.690
We gotta get outta here.
Ooh, we're fancy people.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:55.523
We gotta get outta here.

00:05:55.523 --> 00:05:57.820
We watch movies and talk about 'em.

